1
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:08,130
(Sheldon:)May I point out to you all

2
00:00:08,130 --> 00:00:10,500
(Sheldon:)that the screening is
"first come, first served"?

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,070
Relax, it's 5:00. The movie
doesn't start till midnight.

4
00:00:14,070 --> 00:00:16,440
(Sheldon:)Another way of saying that is

5
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,580
"the movie starts at midnight,
and it's already 5:00."

6
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:19,840
(Sheldon:)Let's go.

7
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:22,080
(Howard:)You know, if we miss it,
we'll have the fun of

8
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,430
(Howard:)listening to Sheldon whine about
it for the rest of our lives.

9
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:28,290
(Sheldon:)See? Howard's on my side.

10
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:29,920
(Howard:)Actually, I'm not.

11
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:31,920
(Howard:)I'm using sarcasm to mock you.

12
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:35,780
(Sheldon:)Drat. Now I'm 8 for 27.

13
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:37,740
(Leonard:)Don't worry, Sheldon.
We'll be fine.

14
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,700
What happened to
the Leonard Hofstadter

15
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:42,070
who waited in line
with me for 14 hours

16
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:44,400
to see the midnight premiere
of Star Trek: Nemesis?

17
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:47,170
Oh. Well, he waited
in line for 14 hours,

18
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:48,770
while you napped
in a lawn chair,

19
00:00:48,770 --> 00:00:50,440
he got in a fight
with a Klingon

20
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:52,140
when he stepped
out of line to pee

21
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:53,910
and you wouldn't wake up
to vouch for him,

22
00:00:53,910 --> 00:00:57,350
and worst of all,
he saw Star Trek: Nemesis.

23
00:00:57,350 --> 00:00:59,480
(Sheldon:)But how were our seats?

24
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:00,550
(Leonard:)Excellent.

25
00:01:00,550 --> 00:01:02,190
(Sheldon:)I rest my case.

